// A recovered record is laid out at its recovered offsets, not at whatever
// natural C layout its member types produce: an unchanged callee reads the
// record where the binary put things.
//
//   gap_rec      1-byte tag, 4-byte value at offset 8: explicit padding
//   packed_rec   4-byte value at offset 1: packed
//   view_rec     a union stays a union, padded to its recovered size
//   tail_rec     16 bytes with one 4-byte member: tail padding
//   outer_rec    a record member is completed before the record holding it
//   bits_rec     bit-field `b` recovered at bit 5; C puts it at bit 3
//   overlap_rec  two struct members share bytes 2-3
//
// The last two cannot be reproduced and are reported, a warning by default and
// an error under -strict.  A PTRSUB offset that names no member (inside
// `word` in overlap_rec) is lifted as byte arithmetic, not as the next member.
//
// RUN: bash %strip-json-comments %s > %t.json
// RUN: %patchir-decomp -input %t.json -emit-llvm -print-tu -output %t > %t.log 2>&1
// RUN: %file-check -vv -check-prefix=WARN %s --input-file %t.log
// RUN: %file-check -vv -check-prefix=C %s --input-file %t.c
// RUN: %file-check -vv -check-prefix=LL %s --input-file %t.ll
// RUN: not %patchir-decomp -input %t.json -emit-llvm -strict -output %t.strict > %t.strict.log 2>&1
// RUN: %file-check -vv -check-prefix=ERR %s --input-file %t.strict.log
// RUN: test ! -e %t.strict.ll
//
